    "body": "How can I solve this error?\r\n\r\nCode:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nself.pipe.unet_garm = torch.compile(self.pipe.unet_garm, mode=\"max-autotune\", fullgraph=True)\r\nself.pipe.unet_vton = torch.compile(self.pipe.unet_vton, mode=\"max-autotune\", fullgraph=True)\r\n```\r\n\r\nError Message:\r\n```bash\r\nNotImplementedError: 'immutable_list' object does not support mutation. If you are attempting to modify the kwargs or args of a torch.fx.Node object,\r\ninstead create a new copy of it and assign the copy to the node:\r\n    new_args = ... # copy and mutate args\r\n    node.args = new_args\r\n```\r\n....\r\n```bash\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/torch/_dynamo/exc.py\", line 193, in unimplemented\r\n    raise Unsupported(msg)\r\ntorch._dynamo.exc.Unsupported: running call_module L__self___down_blocks_0_attentions_0_transformer_blocks_0(*(FakeTensor(..., device='cuda:0', size=(2, 12288, 320), dtype=torch.float16), []), **{'attention_mask': None, 'encoder_hidden_states': FakeTensor(..., device='cuda:0', size=(2, 2, 768), dtype=torch.float16), 'encoder_attention_mask': None, 'timestep': None, 'cross_attention_kwargs': None, 'class_labels': None})\r\n\r\nfrom user code:\r\n   File \".../unet_garm_2d_condition.py\", line 1079, in forward\r\n    sample, res_samples, spatial_attn_inputs = downsample_block(\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1520, in _call_impl\r\n    return forward_call(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \".../unet_garm_2d_blocks.py\", line 1172, in forward\r\n    hidden_states, spatial_attn_inputs = attn(\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.10/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1520, in _call_impl\r\n    return forward_call(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \".../transformer_garm_2d.py\", line 381, in forward\r\n    hidden_states, spatial_attn_inputs = block(\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen I add these parameters it gives an error.\r\n```\r\nmode=\"max-autotune\", fullgraph=True\r\n```",
